    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a public company founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, CA, USA. It trades under the ticker WDAY and reported revenue of 9552000000 USD for the fiscal period ending 2026-01-31 on a 10-K. The company's website describes an enterprise AI platform for HR, finance, and IT, featuring Sana and agentic AI. Workday says its platform can activate teams of specialized agents to perform key processes across HR, finance, and IT, and that its agents can find, build, act, and automate.\n\nWorkday AI is the company's AI product. The product record describes it as covering HR and finance AI, skills-based talent, predictive analytics, and sensitive HR data exposure. The company's site frames its AI as turning AI into ROI faster and delivering outcomes driven by trust, agility, and data readiness.\n\nFederal court records list Workday as a defendant in multiple district court cases, including Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Inc. in the Eastern District of California, Williams v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of Georgia, Elias v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of California, and Hill v. Workday, Inc. in both the District of Maryland and the Eastern District of Virginia.",
